# SABOTAGE: T166 / ADR-050 §4.3 — the OPT-IN conjunct is dropped from
# `Samen.Fleet.PublicStatus.published?/1`, so the public status page renders EVERY
# registered app the moment a host mounts the route. This is the shape the whole
# feature is built to make impossible: `flt_app.publish_status` defaults to `false`
# precisely so that mounting `samen_fleet_status_route/1` on a live cockpit exposes
# an EMPTY page rather than the fleet, and an operator publishes one app at a time
# with `Samen.Fleet.Registry.set_publish_status/4`. With the conjunct gone the
# default silently inverts: a cockpit that registered 30 tenant deployments
# publishes all 30 slugs and their current health to an unauthenticated URL, having
# been asked about none of them.
#
# Flips the named §4.3 red. Everything else stays GREEN, which is what makes the red
# mean what it says: the projection still masks an out-of-shape slug, still maps the
# internal vocabulary to the smaller public one, still excludes deregistered apps,
# and `set_publish_status/4` is still refused for a heartbeat actor — so the red
# fails because the opt-in filter is gone, not because the projection broke.
#
# NOT TOUCHED, deliberately: the `status != :deregistered` half of the same clause
# (a deregistered app must still leave the page — that is not what this proves), the
# fallback `published?(_row)` clause, the slug mask (361 owns it), the rate limit
# (362 owns it) and the fail-closed arm (363 owns it).
#
# Edits ONE pattern in ONE private clause head, so the file still compiles under
# `--warnings-as-errors`: the second clause stays reachable (a row with no `:status`
# key), and no attribute or function goes unused.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/fleet_public_status_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: registering an app does NOT publish it
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/fleet/public_status.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/fleet/public_status.ex
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/fleet/public_status.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/fleet/public_status.ex
@@ -156,7 +156,9 @@ defmodule Samen.Fleet.PublicStatus do
   # Opt-in AND still registered. A deregistered app is not "down" — it is gone, so
   # it leaves the page entirely. Anything that is not literally `true` is unpublished
   # (fail closed: a `nil` from a namespace mid-migration publishes nothing).
-  defp published?(%{publish_status: true, status: status}), do: status != :deregistered
+  # SABOTAGE (T166/ADR-050 §4.3): the OPT-IN conjunct is dropped from the filter —
+  # every registered app is published the moment the route is mounted.
+  defp published?(%{status: status}), do: status != :deregistered
   defp published?(_row), do: false
 
   defp entry(%{slug: slug, status: status}) do
